    "reasoning": "q-122498 is authored as an ordinary fraction, so its mathematical value is 7/6, which is absent from the choices. MA instead interprets that fraction as a binomial coefficient and answers 7; this is a source error. q-85044 uses vertically stacked entries, consistent with binomial notation. The combination answers are: C(6,3)=20, C(20,16)=4845, C(9,3)=84, C(7,5)=21, C(15,10)=3003, and C(80,4)=1581580. For q-124611 and q-124608, x=sqrt(1-y²)>0 gives 2/3 and sqrt(7)/3. Their intermediate steps incorrectly attach ± to a principal square root, but their final answers are correct. For the remaining unit-circle questions, the diagrams place P in quadrant I: q-37915 gives 2(1-10/16)=3/4; q-65059 gives sqrt(1-25/81)=2sqrt(14)/9; q-65062 gives sec(theta)=1/sqrt(1-3/9)=sqrt(6)/2; q-124743 gives csc(theta)=1/sqrt(1-1/9)=3sqrt(2)/4; q-65072 gives tan(theta)=(3/5)/(4/5)=3/4; q-124791 gives tan(theta)=(sqrt(13)/5)/(2sqrt(3)/5)=sqrt(39)/6. For q-100449, equating exponents in base 8 gives 5a-12=-2(a+4), hence a=4/7. Each MA answer below is supported by its own captured solution; no submitted-grade evidence was supplied.",
